{"kind":"assert","text":"IE-1 with FG-1: two facts from the lane, which stopped for the gate at WIP 1c9ad273.\n\n1. The signature in IE-1, `isItemEffect(effect: Effect): effect is ItemEffect`, does not compile (TS2677). `ItemEffect` comes from `GenesisEffect`, and it can hold the encoded self of a genesis draft, so it is not a subtype of `Effect`. The lane gave the guard the parameter `Effect | GenesisEffect`. The guard still takes every `Effect`. A map that `satisfies Record\u003cItemEffect[\"effect\"], true\u003e` ties the guard to the type. A tsc probe showed that each of three drifts fails to compile: a kind missing from the map, a kind added only to the type, and a kind removed only from the type. Unless you rule otherwise, the head keeps this signature, and its note explains it.\n\n2. FG-1 step 2: no caller of applyEntry folds a genesis under another definition on purpose. The production callers are packages/scope/src/turn.ts:515 and packages/replay/src/verify.ts:2591. Both fold under the definition that the seed names, and verify.ts reads it through `#pin`. packages/replay/src/view.ts:44 passes the definition that its caller gives. About 25 callers in tests and examples fold under their fixture's own definition. `genesisJudged` (packages/derive/src/genesis.ts:141) already refuses the same mismatch, so every judged genesis passes the new fold check. The lane went on with the change to fold.ts.\n\nSo far: the two new test files pass 3 of 3, and tsc passes for both derive configs. check-kernel-boundary refuses 0. Not yet run: the derive fold tests and the fold callers' tests. Those wait until the gate ends. item-effects.ts and fold.ts are kernel source, so the head needs the section 7 review."}